## Primary Data Flow: Recipe Input → PDF Output

1. User searches → `GET /api/search?query=` → ranked list (top 40)
2. Selects food → `GET /api/food/{fdc_id}` → `MacroProfile` (per 100g) + `PortionSize[]`
3. `recipeStore.addIngredient(Omit<IngredientItem,"instanceId">)` — assigns UUID `instanceId`
   - `baseMacros` cached per row (raw per-100g, never scaled)
   - `availablePortions` cached so unit picker still works after food detail query is gone
4. `useNutritionCalc()` → `calculateRecipeMacros(ingredients, portionDivisor)` → live `MacroProfile` for label preview
5. "Generate Label" → `POST /api/generate_label` → backend re-fetches DB, recalculates, Jinja2 → WeasyPrint → PDF bytes → browser download

### Backend POST `/api/generate_label` sequence
a. Validate body (≤64 KB; 1–100 ingredients; valid `fdc_id`s; client already flattened portionRef → grams)
b. `database.get_foods_by_ids(fdc_ids)` — batch fetch; 400 if any missing
c. `nutrition.calculate_recipe_macros(...)` → `(unrounded_dict, rounded_MacroProfile)`
d. `pdf.render_label_html(macros, request, unrounded_macros)` — %DV uses **unrounded** (avoid rounding error)
e. `_render_pdf_with_timeout(html)` — `asyncio.Semaphore(2)` + `asyncio.to_thread(generate_pdf)` → bytes (504 on timeout)

